THE GAME

Ultima Underworld II: Labyrinth of Worlds was developed by Looking Glass Technologies and published by Origin Systems in 1993. Its copyright belongs to its owners (Electronic Arts). Ultima and Ultima Underworld are trademarks of Electronic Arts.

The decompiled game code in this repository is derived from the game's program, UW2.EXE. That is the game's C and assembly under src/ (every directory but src/port) with the shared headers in src/include, and the C under src/port that translates or reimplements the game's own assembly modules. The tables in map/, targets/, symbols.tsv and fmtowns/syms.tsv describe UW2.EXE and its FM Towns counterpart. This project claims no ownership of the game, and the MIT licence in LICENSE does not grant any right in it.

No game data is included: no executable, art, sound, map, text or other file of the game, in the repository or in any release package. To build or play anything you need your own copy of the game; the GOG release is the one the tools and the port check for.

THIS PROJECT'S OWN WORK

The MIT licence in LICENSE covers only this project's original work: the tools (tools/, the Makefile and the workflows in .github/), the port's own code under src/port that is not derived from the game, the documentation (docs/ and the README), the tests (tests/) and the comments, names and structure added to the decompiled code. Where a file holds both, the licence applies to this project's contribution only.

EXHUME'S RUNTIME

The port's portability layer, emulated PC hardware, platform layer, sound library and drivers, x86 machine and record and replay code are Exhume's runtime (https://github.com/abedegno/Exhume, runtime/), by the same author under the same MIT licence (LICENSE, the same text), which the builds compile from an Exhume checkout at the commit tools/exhume-ref names; it is not copied into this repository, but it is compiled into the port and its release packages.

OTHER CODE IN THE REPOSITORY

- src/lib/OVERLAY.ASM is Borland's VROOMM overlay manager, rebuilt from OVERLAY.LIB of Turbo C++ 1.01, which UW2.EXE links. Its copyright belongs to its owner (Borland, now Embarcadero). The Turbo C++ and Turbo Assembler programs themselves are not included.
- src/sound/AIL.ASM is the Audio Interface Library API of John Miles (Miles Design), which its author released on 26 May 2000 as freeware "usable by anyone for any purpose, commercial or otherwise, without restriction or limitation", in effect public domain; the port's sound drivers are written from that release (THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES).
